<%# locals: (markdown:) %>
<%# A MARKDOWN FILE'S TWO VIEWS (2026-11-02, the UX audit's D8), rendered by files/show AS A LAYOUT
    around the source viewer it yields. `markdown` is FilesController#show's Maker::MarkdownFile
    answer: nil for anything that is not Markdown, an html for one that rendered, or a problem.

    RENDERED BY DEFAULT, SOURCE ONE PRESS AWAY. The two buttons are the hub's view-toggle shape
    (`.view-toggle .toggle`, `active` for the look and `aria-pressed` for what a screen reader hears),
    and markdown_view_controller.js swaps which pane is hidden. Both panes are server-rendered: the
    source pane is the SAME viewer chain every text file gets, so on an editable file Source is the
    editor exactly as before, mounted while hidden (it fetches its own bytes either way).

    `.markdown` IS THE README CARD'S CLASS, so this prose reads like the card's and the fileopen sweep
    (template_hygiene_test.rb) treats its links as rendered Markdown, which they are.

    NO HTML, NO TOGGLE: an over-cap file, an unreachable library or a file gone since the stat get the
    source view alone, under one sentence saying why (the unreachable one is the app's one sentence,
    FilesController::UNREACHABLE; the layout's banner names the outage itself).

    `editor:saved` IS THE EDITOR TELLING THIS VIEW IT IS STALE: a Save in Source rewrites the file
    without reloading the page, so pressing Rendered after one loads the page again rather than
    showing what the file said before. %>
<% if markdown&.html %>
  <div class="markdown-view" data-controller="markdown-view" data-action="editor:saved->markdown-view#saved">
    <div class="view-toggle markdown-view-toggle" role="group" aria-label="View">
      <% [ [ "rendered", "Rendered" ], [ "source", "Source" ] ].each do |pane, label| %>
        <button type="button" class="toggle<%= " active" if pane == "rendered" %>"
                aria-pressed="<%= pane == "rendered" %>"
                data-markdown-view-target="toggle" data-markdown-view-pane-param="<%= pane %>"
                data-action="markdown-view#show"><%= label %></button>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <div class="markdown markdown-rendered" data-markdown-view-target="pane" data-pane="rendered"><%= markdown.html %></div>
    <div class="markdown-source" data-markdown-view-target="pane" data-pane="source" hidden><%= yield %></div>
  </div>
<% else %>
  <% if markdown&.problem == :too_large %>
    <p class="muted markdown-note">Too large to render; showing the source.</p>
  <% elsif markdown&.problem == :unreachable %>
    <p class="muted markdown-note"><%= FilesController::UNREACHABLE %></p>
  <% end %>
  <%= yield %>
<% end %>
